cidating… [38;2;153;153;153m(3m 41s · ↓ 10.2k tokens · [38;2;255;193;7mdeep in thought with high effort[38;2;153;153;153m)                                                                                                         [38;2;177;185;249m▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔▔[m                                                                                                                                                                                        [38;2;255;193;7m[1m/btw [38;2;153;153;153m[22mwith what you know so far does this app really need a backend, or is it possible to do everything with a frontend only?                                                    [m[22;3H    Technically, yes. With what I've seen[1Cso[1Cfar,[1Ca[1Cfrontend-only[1Capp[1Ccould[1Cdo[1Ceverything[1Cthis[1Cplay[1Cneeds,[1Cand[1Cprobably[1Cthe[1Cnext[1Cplay[1Ctoo.[24;1H [1C   [1m[1CWhy a frontend-only app would work today:[22m[25;7H-[1m[1CThe browser is allowed to fetch the data.[22m[1CThe[1CMetro[1CMondego[1CJSON[1Cis[1Cserved[1Cwith[38;2;177;185;249m[1Caccess-control-allow-origin: *[m,[1Cso[1Cthe[1Cweb[1Capp[1Ccan[1Ccall[1Cit[1Cdirectly.[26;3H    - [1mThe data is small.[22m There are 39 stops and 10 route shapes,[1Cplus[1Ca[1Cfew[1Chundred[1Ctrips[1Cfor[1Ceach[1Cday[1Ctype[1C(452[1Con[1Cweekdays).[1CA[1Cphone[1Ccan[1Ceasily[1Cparse[1Call[1Cof[1Cit[1Cand[1Ckeep[1Cit[1Cin[27;9Hmemory.
 [1C    - [1mAll the logic is pure and cheap.[22m[1CFinding th[1C nearest stop, picking the day type (with [1Che Portuguese [1Colid[1Cy calendar),[1Cplacing bus[1Cs[1Calong[1Cthe[1Cshape[1Cand[1Cworking[1Cout[29;9H"minutes[1Caway"[1Care[1Call[1Csmall[1Ccalculations.[1CThey[1Ccould[1Crun[1Cin[38;2;177;185;249m[1Cpackages/shared[m[1Cor[1Cin[1Cthe[1Cweb[1Capp[1Citself.[30;3H    - [1mOffline and stale data can be handled in the browser.[22m[1CThe[1CPWA[1Cservice[1Cworker[1Ccan[1Ccache[1Cthe[1Clast[1Cgood[1Ccopy[1Cand[1Cshow[1Chow[1Cold[1Cit[1Cis.[31;7H-[1m[1CHosting gets simpler.[22m[1CThe[1Capp[1Cwould[1Cbe[1Cstatic[1Cfiles,[1Cso[1Cit[1Ccan[1Cgo[1Con[1Cany[1Cfree[1Cstatic[1Chost[1Cwith[1Cno[1Cserver[1Cto[1Crun.[1CSince[1Cthe[1Cdeployment[1Cchoice[1Chas[1Cbeen[1Cdeferred,[1Cthat's[1Ca
 [1C   [1C  real advantage.[1C                                                                                                                                                            [34;1H      [1mWhat the backend buys you (why tech.md has one):[22m
      1. [1mThe live feed.[22m The Agit Planner real-time API is the unknown. I don't know whether it allows browser requests (CORS), whether it needs an API key you'd have to keep       [36;6H    secret, or how easy its GTFS-RT protobuf[1Cis[1Cto[1Chandle[1Cin[1Cthe[1Cbrowser.[1CAny[1Cone[1Cof[1Cthose[1Ccould[1Cforce[1Ca[1Cserver[1Clater.[37;6H 2. [1mProtection from an unstable source.[22m The timetable JSON is undocumented and may change without notice. With the backend, one adapter shields every client,[1Cand[1Cyou[1Ccan[1Cfix[38;10Ha[1Cformat[1Cchange[1Con[1Cthe[1Cserver[1Cwithout[1Cusers[1Chaving[1Cto[1Cpick[1Cup[1Ca[1Cnew[1Capp[1Cversion.[1CA[1Cstatic[1Capp[1Ccan[1Cbe[1Credeployed[1Cquickly[1Ctoo,[1Cbut[1Ccached[1CPWA[1Ccopies[1Cmay[1Ckeep[1Cthe[1Cbroken
 [1C       parser until [1Chey upd[1Ct[1C.[K
      3. [1mLoad on a third party.[22m Without a backend, every phone polls Metro Mondego's host directly. With one, your server fetches once and serves the cached copy to everyone.[1CFor[41;6H    an unofficial, unlicensed source, being a polite client matters.                                                                                                           [42;7H4.[1m[1CDoing the work once.[22m[1CBus[1Cestimates[1Cand[1CETAs[1Care[1Ccomputed[1Ca[1Csingle[1Ctime[1Cinstead[1Cof[1Con[1Cevery[1Cdevice.[1CThat[1Cmatters[1Cmore[1Conce[1Cpositions[1Cupdate[1Cevery[1Cfew[1Cseconds.
[K
      [1mMy take:[22m the backend isn't needed yet, but reason 1 is the one most likely to make you need it later. A reasonable middle ground is to put all the logic in [38;2;177;185;249mpackages/shared[m,  [45;7Hso[1Cit[1Cruns[1Canywhere,[1Cand[1Ckeep[1Cthe[1CAPI[1Cthin.[1CThen[1Cdropping[1Cthe[1Cbackend,[1Cor[1Cadding[1Cit[1Cback,[1Ccosts[1Clittle.[46;5H                                                                                                                                                                                [47;7HKeep[1Cin[1Cmind[1Cthat[1Ctech.md[1Ccurrently[1Crequires[1Cthe[1Cbackend[1C("the[1Cweb[1Capp[1Cnever[1Ccalls[1Cthird-party[1Cdata[1Csources[1Cdirectly").[1CThe[1Cplan[1CI'm[1Cwriting[1Cfollows[1Cthat,[1Cand[1Conly[1Cthe[48;7HArchitect can[1Cchange[1Ctech.md.[1CIf[1Cyou[1Cwant[1Cto[1Cgo[1Cfrontend-only,[1Csay[1Cso[1Cin[1Cthe[1Cmain[1Cconversation[1Cbefore[1Cthe[1Cplan[1Cis[1Capproved,[1Cand[1Cthe[1CArchitect[1Ccan[1Cupdate[1Ctech.md[1Cfirst.[38;2;153;153;153m[50;5H↑/↓[4Cscroll · c to copy · f to fork · Esc to close[m[38;2;153;153;153m[17;21H2[m[38;2;255;193;7m[1m✢[m]0;◐ Play 001 project structure plan[38;2;255;193;7m[1m*[m[38;2;153;153;153m[13;1H [m[38;2;255;193;7m[1m[17;1H✶[m[38;2;255;193;7m[1m✻[m[38;2;255;193;7m[1m✽[m[38;2;153;153;153m[13;1H●[m[38;2;153;153;153m[17;21H3[m[38;2;255;193;7m[1m✻[m]0;◑ Play 001 project structure plan[38;2;255;193;7m[1m✶[m[38;2;255;193;7m[1m*[m[38;2;153;153;153m[13;1H [38;2;255;193;7m[1m[17;1H✢[m[38;2;255;193;7m[1m·[m[38;2;153;153;153m[19C4[m[38;2;255;193;7m[1m✢[m]0;◐ Play 001 project structure plan[38;2;153;153;153m[13;1H●[m[38;2;255;193;7m[1m[17;1H*[m[38;2;255;193;7m[1m✶[m[38;2;255;193;7m[1m✻[m[38;2;153;153;153m[13;1H [m[38;2;255;193;7m[1m[17;1H✽[m[38;2;153;153;153m[19C5[m]0;◑ Play 001 project structure plan[38;2;255;193;7m[1m✻[m